{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2292","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2292","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2292\",\"parent_revision\":\"0d8a870c23a5c4fcbb11ceb19dfeb8d17fb69864\",\"root_revision\":\"a22838a8900b79d3af302d2dcf348b0b766d529c0c0350645813b93df9f556bc\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Refactor\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe backlog MCP server (`backlog_core/server.py`) exposes 42 individual tools. Each tool appears as a separate entry in agent `tools:` declarations and consumes context window space in every agent that loads the full tool set. Agents currently hold inconsistent subsets \u2014 some have 0 backlog tools, some have 14, one has 42 \u2014 with no systematic basis for which subset is correct.\\n\\nThe SAM MCP server exposes 3 tools total (`sam_plan`, `sam_task`, `sam_active_task`), each accepting an `action` discriminator with Pydantic-validated payloads:\\n\\n```\\n# SAM: 3 tools covering equivalent operations\\nsam_plan(config={\\\"action\\\": \\\"list\\\"})\\nsam_plan(config={\\\"action\\\": \\\"create\\\", \\\"slug\\\": \\\"...\\\", \\\"goal\\\": \\\"...\\\", \\\"tasks\\\": [...]})\\nsam_plan(config={\\\"action\\\": \\\"status\\\"}, plan=\\\"P42\\\")\\nsam_task(config={\\\"action\\\": \\\"claim\\\"}, plan=\\\"P42\\\", task=\\\"T1\\\")\\nsam_task(config={\\\"action\\\": \\\"state\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"complete\\\"}, plan=\\\"P42\\\", task=\\\"T1\\\")\\n\\n# Backlog: 42 tools for equivalent operations\\nbacklog_list(...)\\nbacklog_view(...)\\nbacklog_add(...)\\nbacklog_update(...)\\nbacklog_close(...)\\nbacklog_resolve(...)\\n# ... 36 more\\n```\\n\\nThe inconsistency between the two servers makes the tool access model harder to reason about, requires agents to declare long explicit tool lists, and bloats the context window before any work begins.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **maintainer of the codebase**, I want to **backlog mcp server exposes 42 flat tools instead of consolidated action-based pattern** so that **the code is cleaner and more maintainable**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation during #2284 quality gate, 2026-05-15\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-05-15\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-05-18)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n7/10 \u2014 Context window pollution affects every agent that loads backlog tools. With 40 flat entries vs 3 for SAM, the tool declaration overhead is 13x higher. This directly degrades agent performance on every task that touches the backlog. However, the refactor has non-trivial scope: all 21 agent files that reference backlog tools need `tools:` declaration updates, and #473 creates merge coordination risk.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- **Blocks**: No downstream items are blocked by the current state\\n- **Bottleneck**: Agent `tools:` declarations \u2014 21 agent files must list individual tool names; any new tool added to the server requires manually updating each agent\\n- **Context window tax**: Each agent that loads all 40 backlog tools consumes ~2-3x more context budget on tool schema declarations compared to the SAM pattern\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Reduces tool declaration overhead in agent frontmatter from 40+ entries to ~4-6 consolidated tool names\\n- Makes the access model predictable and learnable \u2014 one consolidated tool per semantic domain mirrors the SAM precedent\\n- New operations added to the server do not require agent `tools:` updates when the operation fits within an existing consolidated tool's action set\\n- Eliminates the inconsistency problem: agents currently hold 0, 7, or 42 backlog tools with no systematic basis for which subset is correct\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nThe backlog MCP server exposes a small set of consolidated tools (modeled after `sam_plan`, `sam_task`, `sam_active_task`). Each consolidated tool accepts an `action` discriminator field with a Pydantic-validated config payload. Agents declare a short list of consolidated tool names in `tools:`. The full operation set remains accessible \u2014 nothing is removed, only the registration surface changes.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\n**4 consolidated tools** (decided 2026-05-23):\\n\\n| Consolidated tool | Actions covered | Notes |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `backlog` | list, view, add, update, groom, close, resolve, sync, pull, normalize, strike_entry, list_milestones, create_milestone, get_soonest_milestone, list_issues, comment_issue, list_comments, read_comment | Generic operations; milestone/comment/issue actions move behind BacklogBackend Protocol so all backends implement them |\\n| `dispatch` | read, validate, stale_check, create_plan, conflicts, wave_start, item_status, wave_status, spawn | Wave orchestration \u2014 unchanged grouping |\\n| `artifact` | register, list, get, read, migrate | Artifact lifecycle \u2014 unchanged grouping |\\n| `sam_integration` | create_sam_task, get_sam_tasks, update_sam_task_status, get_ready_sam_tasks | SAM task bridge \u2014 separate group for clean separation |\\n\\n**Excluded from this refactor \u2014 GitHub-native tools:**\\n\\n`backlog_list_labels`, `backlog_list_merged_prs`, `backlog_list_projects`, `backlog_create_project` are GitHub-native concepts (PR, label taxonomy, GitHub Projects board) with no equivalent in other backends. They do not belong in a multi-backend backlog tool. Follow-on: add a CLI interface using the existing GitHub API for these operations (tracked separately).\\n\\n**Standalone (not consolidated):**\\n\\n`profile_load`, `profile_list` \u2014 from `agent_profile/server.py`, exposed under the backlog namespace. Keep as standalone tools; not in scope for this refactor.\\n\\n**Files:**\\n\\n- `backlog_core/server.py` \u2014 replace all flat `@mcp.tool` registrations with 4 action-discriminated consolidated tools\\n- `backlog_core/action_models.py` (new) \u2014 Pydantic discriminated union models per consolidated tool, mirroring `sam_schema/core/action_models.py` pattern\\n- All agent `.md` files under `plugins/development-harness/agents/` with `mcp__plugin_dh_backlog__` entries \u2014 update to consolidated tool names\\n- Any other skills, docs, or config files that reference flat `mcp__plugin_dh_backlog__*` tool names \u2014 full repo-wide search required (see Acceptance Criteria)\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `grep -c \\\"@mcp.tool\\\" plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` returns 4 or fewer (the 4 consolidated tools, plus `profile_load`/`profile_list` which stay as-is)\\n2. Every operation in the current 40 flat tools \u2014 **excluding** `backlog_list_labels`, `backlog_list_merged_prs`, `backlog_list_projects`, `backlog_create_project` \u2014 remains callable via the consolidated tools with no capability regression\\n3. `backlog_list_labels`, `backlog_list_merged_prs`, `backlog_list_projects`, `backlog_create_project` are removed from `server.py`; a follow-on item tracks their CLI replacement\\n4. `backlog_core/action_models.py` exists and defines Pydantic discriminated union models for each of the 4 consolidated tools\\n5. Milestone, comment, and issue operations (`list_milestones`, `create_milestone`, `get_soonest_milestone`, `list_issues`, `comment_issue`, `list_comments`, `read_comment`) are implemented behind the `BacklogBackend` Protocol so non-GitHub backends can implement them\\n6. **Repo-wide reference update**: `grep -r \\\"mcp__plugin_dh_backlog__\\\" .` returns only consolidated tool names \u2014 no flat tool names remain in any agent `.md` file, skill `.md` file, rule, config, or documentation file\\n7. All 21 agent files that previously referenced flat `mcp__plugin_dh_backlog__` tool names have updated `tools:` declarations with the consolidated names\\n8. `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/tests/ -x` passes\\n9. `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/tests/ -x` passes (integration tests)\\n10. MCP server starts and lists consolidated tools: `FASTMCP_SHOW_SERVER_BANNER=false FASTMCP_LOG_ENABLED=false uv run fastmcp list --command \\\"uv run --script plugins/development-harness/scripts/run_backlog_server.py\\\"` returns 6 or fewer tool entries (`backlog`, `dispatch`, `artifact`, `sam_integration`, `profile_load`, `profile_list`)\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|---|---|\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py` \u2014 3-tool consolidated reference implementation |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/action_models.py` \u2014 Pydantic discriminated union pattern |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` \u2014 current flat-tool implementation (40 tools) |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/agent_profile/server.py` \u2014 `profile_load`, `profile_list` tools routed via backlog server |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_server.py` \u2014 existing test coverage |\\n| Agent | `@dh:impact-analyst` \u2014 used to map blast radius |\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- **#473** (MCP prompts + guided elicitation): not a sequencing dependency. #473 is additive-only and blocked on #472 + #465; not actively modifying `server.py`. When #473 resumes, its new tools must be implemented in the consolidated action-based pattern. This item (#2292) should complete first so #473 inherits the correct pattern.\\n- **Follow-on item needed**: New CLI tool for GitHub-native operations (`list_labels`, `list_merged_prs`, `list_projects`, `create_project`) using the existing GitHub API. Not a dependency for this item \u2014 #2292 removes these tools; the follow-on provides the replacement interface.\\n- **Blocks**: Completing this refactor unblocks a clean `tools:` model for all agents and eliminates the inconsistency between agent subsets of backlog tools.\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nMedium \u2014 The SAM pattern provides a clear reference implementation. The primary work is: (1) designing the action groupings and writing Pydantic discriminated union models, (2) refactoring 40 `@mcp.tool` handlers into action-dispatched consolidated handlers, (3) updating 21 agent files. Test update is mechanical. The risk is in the coordination with #473 and in ensuring no operation is lost during consolidation.\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\n- **#473 conflict risk is lower than originally assessed.** #473 is additive-only (adds 5 `@mcp.prompt` and 4 async `@mcp.tool` functions \u2014 no existing tools modified or removed). It is also blocked on its own prerequisites: #472 (async tool conversion) and #465 (context logging), both still open. The plan artifact for #473 was written when server.py had 10 tools; the server now has 40, so the plan is stale against the current codebase. #473 is not actively in flight. Decision: start #2292 now. When #473 eventually resumes, new additions must conform to the consolidated tool pattern established here.\\n- **GitHub-specific tools architectural decision made (2026-05-23):** The 4 tools that are GitHub-native (`backlog_list_labels`, `backlog_list_merged_prs`, `backlog_list_projects`, `backlog_create_project`) are out of scope for the backlog MCP server entirely. They do not belong in a multi-backend tool. They will be mapped to a new CLI interface using the existing GitHub API (see follow-on item). This unblocks the grouping decision \u2014 see Desired Structure.\\n\\n### Impact Radius\\n\\n| System | Impact | Risk |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `backlog_core/server.py` | Primary change \u2014 all 40 flat `@mcp.tool` registrations replaced with 4 consolidated; 4 GitHub-native tools removed entirely | High \u2014 server behavior must be fully preserved for the 36 kept operations |\\n| `backlog_core/action_models.py` (new file) | New Pydantic discriminated union models for each consolidated tool | Low \u2014 net new, no existing code affected |\\n| `BacklogBackend` Protocol (`backlog_core/backend_protocol.py`) | Milestone, comment, and issue operations move from GitHub-specific implementations to protocol methods \u2014 all backends must implement them | Medium \u2014 SQLite and memory backends need new method implementations |\\n| All agent `.md` files with `mcp__plugin_dh_backlog__` entries | `tools:` frontmatter updated to consolidated names | Medium \u2014 21 files confirmed; grep may reveal more in other locations |\\n| **Repo-wide**: skills, rules, docs, configs | Any file referencing flat `mcp__plugin_dh_backlog__*` tool names must be updated | Medium \u2014 scope larger than 21 agent files; full `grep -r` required at start of implementation |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_server.py` | Test suite targets current flat tool signatures \u2014 requires update | High \u2014 tests break until updated |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_integration_reconciliation.py` | May reference tool names \u2014 verify | Medium |\\n| `agent_profile/server.py` | `profile_load`/`profile_list` stay standalone \u2014 no change needed | None |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/scripts/run_backlog_server.py` | Runner script \u2014 no change expected; verify after refactor | Low |\\n| GitHub-native tools (removed) | `backlog_list_labels`, `backlog_list_merged_prs`, `backlog_list_projects`, `backlog_create_project` removed from server; follow-on CLI covers these via existing GitHub API | Low for this item \u2014 follow-on item carries the risk |\\n| Plugin cache in `~/.claude/plugins/cache/` | Version bump required; agents loading stale cache see old flat tools | Medium \u2014 operational concern post-deploy |\\n| #473 (MCP prompts + guided elicitation) | Additive-only; blocked on #472 and #465; not actively in flight. When #473 resumes, new additions must follow the consolidated pattern established here | Low \u2014 coordinate at that point |\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\n**issue-classification**: refactor\\n\\nThe backlog MCP server accumulated flat tool registrations organically as features were added. The SAM server was designed from the start with consolidated action-discriminated tools. This is an unbounded-design artifact: no boundary was drawn at design time on how many tools could be added, so the server grew to 40 flat tools without friction.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Output / Evidence\\n\\n- Count flat tools: `grep -c \\\"@mcp\\\\.tool\\\" plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` returns 40\\n- Compare: `grep \\\"@mcp\\\\.tool\\\" plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py` returns 3 entries\\n- Agent inconsistency: `grep -c \\\"mcp__plugin_dh_backlog__\\\" plugins/development-harness/agents/impact-analyst.md` shows 42 individual tool entries vs `grep -c \\\"mcp__plugin_dh_backlog__\\\" plugins/development-harness/agents/backlog-item-groomer.md` shows 7\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Questions for Human\\n\\nAll questions resolved 2026-05-23:\\n\\n| Question | Decision |\\n|---|---|\\n| Consolidated tool count and grouping | **4 tools**: `backlog`, `dispatch`, `artifact`, `sam_integration` \u2014 see Desired Structure |\\n| GitHub-specific tools (`list_labels`, `list_merged_prs`, `list_projects`, `create_project`) | **Out of scope** \u2014 not a backlog concern; map to separate CLI tool using existing GitHub API |\\n| Backward compatibility | **Breaking change accepted** \u2014 update all agent files and any other references to flat `mcp__plugin_dh_backlog__*` names |\\n| `profile_load` / `profile_list` | **Stay standalone** \u2014 not consolidated in this refactor |\\n| #473 conflict | **Start #2292 now** \u2014 #473 is additive-only and blocked on its own prerequisites; not actively in flight |\\n\\n### RT-ICA Assessment\\n\\n**Verdict: APPROVED-WITH-GAPS**\\n\\n| Input | Status | Notes |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Functional intent | AVAILABLE | Consolidate flat tools into action-discriminated pattern matching SAM server |\\n| Scope boundaries | PARTIAL | Number of consolidated tools and grouping strategy not specified; 4+ semantic groups exist |\\n| External interfaces | AVAILABLE | SAM `action_models.py` pattern is the reference implementation; fully readable |\\n| Constraints | PARTIAL | Backward-compatibility requirement not stated; 21 agent files need `tools:` updates; #473 in-progress modifies same file |\\n| Existing system context | AVAILABLE | 40 `@mcp.tool` decorators confirmed in `backlog_core/server.py` (description says 42 \u2014 minor count drift) |\\n| Verification expectations | MISSING | Acceptance criteria is a placeholder; no concrete \\\"done\\\" definition |\\n\\nMissing inputs requiring unblock tasks or human clarification:\\n1. Target consolidated tool count and action-group boundary design\\n2. Backward-compatibility policy (agent `tools:` declarations in 21 files must change)\\n3. Coordination strategy with #473 (MCP prompts + guided elicitation \u2014 in-progress, same file)\\n\\n---\\n\",\"digest\":\"b87654908778b7a39b71eb2a18fc5f7a09b58e8159896450738b1eb5dc6f0917\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPg2rIw\"}"}